1
00:00:01,334 --> 00:00:02,376
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:04,629
- "He says his name is Patrick Jane."
- Never met him.

3
00:00:04,754 --> 00:00:06,881
- Did he say why he came in?
- Just that he wants to talk to you.

4
00:00:07,006 --> 00:00:08,049
Mr. Jane!

5
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,676
"Teresa Lisbon, it's nice to meet you."

6
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:14,263
We always thought that you and Lisbon
would, you know, get together.

7
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,806
Jane and Lisbon, yeah right.

8
00:00:16,015 --> 00:00:18,392
- And voila.
- So you're gonna build us a house?

9
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:19,894
- It's a start.
- I need to know

10
00:00:20,019 --> 00:00:22,271
- that you're committed to this, to us.
- I am.

11
00:00:22,396 --> 00:00:23,981
Then are you gonna take off
your wedding ring?

12
00:00:24,148 --> 00:00:26,150
I have a guy who's saying things
about the murders.

13
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:28,152
- Well, what is he saying Wylie?
- He's a psychic.

14
00:00:28,277 --> 00:00:30,112
I saw that the killer's gonna
kill again, tonight.

15
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:32,615
"Why would the killer care
if Gabriel was a real psychic?"

16
00:00:32,823 --> 00:00:35,826
"He wants one for some reason
and Gabriel didn't pass the test."

17
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:37,995
"Welcome back to Austin Today.
I'm Dan Glover."

18
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:41,082
{\an8}"And with me is Patrick Jane,
a psychic who works with the FBI."

19
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:43,626
{\an8}I'm just trying to help my colleagues
understand this man.

20
00:00:43,751 --> 00:00:47,255
- "How would you describe him?"
- "I would say that he's obviously angry"

21
00:00:47,421 --> 00:00:49,173
"probably in a lot of pain."

22
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:50,883
Lazarus. Interesting name.

23
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:52,969
- "He rose from the dead."
- So I hear.

24
00:00:55,429 --> 00:00:59,058
I saw you on TV.
You said you know things.

25
00:00:59,767 --> 00:01:00,810
He's in there.

26
00:01:12,196 --> 00:01:13,906
Jane... Hey.

27
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:17,535
Can you stand up?

28
00:01:34,635 --> 00:01:36,220
- You Agent Tork?
- Yeah.

29
00:01:36,345 --> 00:01:37,388
You guys done looking around in there?

30
00:01:37,513 --> 00:01:38,848
'Cause we're just sitting
on our hands out here.

31
00:01:39,015 --> 00:01:40,683
There's nothing we could find.
It's a mess in there.

32
00:01:40,808 --> 00:01:45,021
But the structure's sound.
Your people can go in. Have fun.

33
00:01:45,938 --> 00:01:47,106
Thanks.

34
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:50,067
All right, listen up.

35
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:53,112
It's been reported there are two bodies
in the basement of this house.

36
00:01:53,237 --> 00:01:56,449
There may also be evidence
pertaining to as many as 10 homicides

37
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:59,452
committed by the recently deceased
individual known as Lazarus.

38
00:01:59,744 --> 00:02:01,454
Real name Joseph Keller.

39
00:02:01,662 --> 00:02:03,414
We wanna put these cases to bed

40
00:02:03,581 --> 00:02:05,583
so that means break out
the fine-toothed combs.

41
00:02:05,958 --> 00:02:07,293
Let's go.

42
00:03:03,599 --> 00:03:04,934
How's your head?

43
00:03:05,893 --> 00:03:07,353
- Oh, hey.
- Hi.

44
00:03:07,853 --> 00:03:08,896
It's fine.

45
00:03:09,021 --> 00:03:10,981
Ears are still ringing a little
but, uh...

46
00:03:11,857 --> 00:03:13,609
just getting ready for the remodel.

47
00:03:13,818 --> 00:03:16,278
- I brought sandwiches.
- Those are the magic words.

48
00:03:16,445 --> 00:03:17,530
Come with me.

49
00:03:29,375 --> 00:03:32,962
Is it me, or does it seem like
the house slants a little bit to the left?

50
00:03:35,131 --> 00:03:36,507
Optical illusion.

51
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:41,429
You're not wearing
your wedding ring.

52
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:43,597
I'm not married.

53
00:03:48,769 --> 00:03:50,896
The ground is slanty,
so it makes the structure

54
00:03:51,021 --> 00:03:53,649
look like it's leaning,
but it is, in fact, not.

55
00:03:54,066 --> 00:03:55,693
It's just an optical illusion.

56
00:03:56,402 --> 00:03:58,571
- Slanty, huh?
- Yeah.

57
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,115
Technical term.

58
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:15,880
This ring has been with me
for a very long time, and, uh...

59
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:22,386
it has obvious significance
with my past.

60
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:29,894
It also represents...

61
00:04:32,396 --> 00:04:33,814
meeting you.

62
00:04:34,398 --> 00:04:37,985
If I didn't have this ring,
I would never have met you.

63
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:40,738
So in a sense, uh...

64
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:45,367
it has the potential to represent
my future, as well.

65
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:51,165
And I-I'm not expecting
you would ever wear it, but...

66
00:04:51,999 --> 00:04:53,667
I wanna share it with you

67
00:04:54,835 --> 00:04:56,045
and...

68
00:04:57,922 --> 00:05:02,885
I want it to represent our future...
together.

69
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,767
I want you to be my wife.

70
00:05:13,813 --> 00:05:15,314
Will you marry me?

71
00:05:19,443 --> 00:05:20,694
Okay.

72
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:23,781
- Yes, yes.
- Yes?

73
00:05:24,031 --> 00:05:25,074
Excellent.

74
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:28,869
I'm glad that's dealt with.
I was a little nervous.

75
00:05:29,119 --> 00:05:30,955
Oh, come on. You knew
I was gonna say yes.

76
00:05:31,288 --> 00:05:34,291
No, even after all these years,
you're still a mystery to me.

77
00:05:34,416 --> 00:05:36,752
- I am?
- Thank you.

78
00:05:55,477 --> 00:05:57,437
Hey, guys, how's the Lazarus case going?

79
00:05:57,563 --> 00:05:59,106
Keller's house is being processed
right now.

80
00:05:59,231 --> 00:06:01,441
Tork's on the scene.
We're just squaring away the paperwork.

81
00:06:01,567 --> 00:06:04,152
Oh, good. Good, good, good.
All right.

82
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,947
Do you guys need anything? Can I help?

83
00:06:07,239 --> 00:06:09,157
Mm... No, not really.

84
00:06:10,242 --> 00:06:13,078
Look, you know, old job's over.

85
00:06:13,245 --> 00:06:16,540
New job hasn't begun. You know,
I'm just spinning my wheels here.

86
00:06:17,708 --> 00:06:19,084
- Hey.
- Hey, guys.

87
00:06:20,085 --> 00:06:24,506
So, um... we wanted you
to be the first to know.

88
00:06:25,257 --> 00:06:27,217
Um... yeah.

89
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:29,803
We're getting married.

90
00:06:29,970 --> 00:06:31,513
Hey!

91
00:06:32,431 --> 00:06:33,849
- I told you.
- No, you didn't.

92
00:06:34,266 --> 00:06:36,310
{\an8}- Congratulations.
- Oh, man!

93
00:06:36,602 --> 00:06:37,644
{\an8}- That's wonderful.
- That's awesome.

94
00:06:37,769 --> 00:06:38,812
{\an8}- Thank you.
- When's the big day?

95
00:06:38,937 --> 00:06:41,773
{\an8}Eh, no big day.
I don't want any wedding fuss.

96
00:06:41,899 --> 00:06:45,152
Oh, we're just gonna slip away quietly
in the next couple of days.

97
00:06:46,445 --> 00:06:47,487
{\an8}All right.

98
00:06:50,115 --> 00:06:54,411
"It's not unusual to be loved
by anyone"

99
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:58,707
{\an8}"it's not unusual to have fun
with anyone"

100
00:07:00,542 --> 00:07:03,879
{\an8}"But when I see you
hanging around with anyone"

101
00:07:05,881 --> 00:07:09,051
{\an8}"It's not unusual to see me cry"

102
00:07:10,594 --> 00:07:11,678
"I wanna die"

103
00:07:15,223 --> 00:07:17,059
{\an8}- "Hi. How are you?"
- "Good. How are you?"

104
00:07:17,184 --> 00:07:18,226
{\an8}"Good."

105
00:07:19,353 --> 00:07:23,690
{\an8}"But when I see you out
and about, it's such a crime"

106
00:07:25,359 --> 00:07:27,986
{\an8}"If you should ever wanna be
loved by anyone"

107
00:07:28,111 --> 00:07:29,655
{\an8}- Thank you. Have a nice day.
- Thank you.

108
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:33,909
"It's not unusual, it happens every day"

109
00:07:34,076 --> 00:07:35,911
Oh, my lord. Sir?

110
00:07:36,995 --> 00:07:38,038
{\an8}I'm good.

111
00:07:39,539 --> 00:07:41,667
That darn barbecue, I swear.

112
00:07:47,839 --> 00:07:50,050
These are two for one, right?

113
00:07:53,470 --> 00:07:56,223
{\an8}- "Hey-hey! Hey!"
- "That's awesome!"

114
00:07:56,598 --> 00:07:58,517
"Hey, even this guy's happy
about it, right?"

115
00:07:58,642 --> 00:07:59,685
"Yeah, congrats."

116
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:03,105
{\an8}- Oh, hi! Hey!
- "Hey."

117
00:08:03,397 --> 00:08:05,524
{\an8}- "Congratulations!"
- "Somebody went number two."

118
00:08:05,983 --> 00:08:07,567
- Thanks.
- "Yeah. All right."

119
00:08:07,693 --> 00:08:09,820
"So, anyway, did you tell uh--
did you tell Tommy yet?"

120
00:08:09,945 --> 00:08:11,738
{\an8}Eh, he's chasing a bail jumper
in Alaska.

121
00:08:11,863 --> 00:08:12,948
{\an8}I left him a message.

122
00:08:13,198 --> 00:08:14,449
{\an8}"Eh, well, you snooze, you lose."

123
00:08:14,574 --> 00:08:16,284
{\an8}"We're gonna miss him
at the bachelor party, though."

124
00:08:16,410 --> 00:08:18,036
{\an8}There is no bachelor party.

125
00:08:18,203 --> 00:08:19,746
{\an8}We're getting married
the day after tomorrow

126
00:08:19,871 --> 00:08:22,124
{\an8}just me and Jane
and the Justice of the Peace.

127
00:08:22,249 --> 00:08:23,792
{\an8}No big wedding, no guests.

128
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:28,714
{\an8}"But... family, right?"

129
00:08:28,839 --> 00:08:30,507
- "Yeah, family."
- "Yeah."

130
00:08:30,632 --> 00:08:33,218
{\an8}No, it's just us.
We wanna get married quietly.

131
00:08:33,468 --> 00:08:35,721
"Well, so, we'll be quiet.
But we're gonna be there, T."

132
00:08:35,846 --> 00:08:37,597
- "I mean, no argument."
- "Hey, Stan, hold it."

133
00:08:37,764 --> 00:08:40,434
"It's her deal, her choice.
You know, she wants to do it that way"

134
00:08:40,559 --> 00:08:43,478
{\an8}- "then let her do it."
- "What are you saying, you mook?"

135
00:08:43,603 --> 00:08:44,646
{\an8}Guys, come on!

136
00:08:44,896 --> 00:08:46,481
"If we're not there, Mom's gonna spin
in her grave"

137
00:08:46,606 --> 00:08:48,108
- "like a freaking crankshaft."
- "Oh, my God."

138
00:08:48,233 --> 00:08:50,318
"She'll be crying for shame
that our sister, our only sister--"

139
00:08:50,444 --> 00:08:53,864
{\an8}"Oh, would you can it, please, Stan?
Teresa just said she don't us there."

140
00:08:53,989 --> 00:08:55,991
{\an8}"Why would you wanna be there
if she doesn't want us there?"

141
00:08:56,116 --> 00:08:58,201
- "I mean--"
- "You're a sad, bitter man, Jimmy Lisbon."

142
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:00,954
- "Well, I-I smile through it."
- "Don't you ever--"

143
00:09:01,079 --> 00:09:02,664
- "I smile through the sadness."
- "Stop it. He's doing it again."

144
00:09:02,789 --> 00:09:04,291
- "I got stronger, though."
- "Ever since he was a little kid--"

145
00:09:04,624 --> 00:09:07,377
- "It's just-- it cuts to the airflow!"
- "Yeah."

146
00:09:34,279 --> 00:09:36,198
- Don't worry.
- Don't worry about what?

147
00:09:36,323 --> 00:09:37,532
You're worried that I'm gonna be upset

148
00:09:37,657 --> 00:09:39,951
because you invited your brothers
to our marriage.

149
00:09:40,077 --> 00:09:41,661
- How did you know that?
- When we're married

150
00:09:41,787 --> 00:09:43,622
do you think you might stop
asking that question?

151
00:09:43,747 --> 00:09:46,124
- It's okay, isn't it?
- They're family.

152
00:09:46,249 --> 00:09:48,418
Thank you. It means a lot to them.

153
00:09:48,543 --> 00:09:49,586
Of course.

154
00:09:52,089 --> 00:09:54,716
Since my brothers are coming
it feels funny

155
00:09:54,841 --> 00:09:57,219
not to invite just a couple
of members from the team.

156
00:09:58,595 --> 00:10:00,013
No, no. You know what? You're right.

157
00:10:00,138 --> 00:10:02,599
We should keep it small.
Small. Just my brothers.

158
00:10:02,849 --> 00:10:04,810
Eh, fine. Invite away.

159
00:10:05,393 --> 00:10:08,480
We're gonna need a few more guests
just to dilute the alcohol content.

160
00:10:08,605 --> 00:10:10,482
- Thank you.
- Just three or four, though.

161
00:10:11,316 --> 00:10:12,526
Where do we draw the line?

162
00:10:12,651 --> 00:10:14,861
Well, that's why we decided
not to invite anyone.

163
00:10:14,986 --> 00:10:17,697
I know. I know. I'm sorry. It's just--
here we are.

164
00:10:17,823 --> 00:10:19,741
- Here we are.
- What?

165
00:10:21,701 --> 00:10:24,121
Oh, look, I'm just gonna surrender
to fate, all right?

166
00:10:24,246 --> 00:10:26,957
So be it.
Big, huge, massive wedding.

167
00:10:27,207 --> 00:10:31,962
No, just 8 or 9 very close friends
at the courthouse-- 9 or 10

168
00:10:32,087 --> 00:10:34,381
and then we can go
to O'Malley's bar afterwards.

169
00:10:34,714 --> 00:10:36,299
12 tops.

170
00:10:36,967 --> 00:10:38,718
Or we could go to a restaurant.
No big deal.

171
00:10:38,844 --> 00:10:40,137
It's not like we're hiring a caterer.

172
00:10:40,262 --> 00:10:43,682
- We don't have a gift registry or anything.
- Sure. Okay.

173
00:10:44,057 --> 00:10:46,143
- Where are you going?
- Well, I have to get you a ring.

174
00:10:46,268 --> 00:10:49,229
- I already have one.
- That is for us.

175
00:10:49,604 --> 00:10:51,356
You need one for you.

176
00:10:51,481 --> 00:10:52,899
- I do?
- You do.

177
00:10:53,567 --> 00:10:55,152
All right, well, shouldn't I come
with you?

178
00:10:55,277 --> 00:10:56,361
Isn't that how you're supposed
to do it?

179
00:10:56,486 --> 00:10:58,905
No, I think we'll waste time bickering.
Besides, I have better taste.

180
00:10:59,072 --> 00:11:00,365
- You think you do.
- You'll see.

181
00:11:01,491 --> 00:11:03,785
- N-nothing too gauche.
- Bye!

182
00:11:05,495 --> 00:11:06,955
- Hey, boss.
- Hey.

183
00:11:08,123 --> 00:11:10,375
The less I have to do,
the more coffee I drink.

184
00:11:10,667 --> 00:11:13,378
So, do you and Lena wanna come
and watch us get married?

185
00:11:13,587 --> 00:11:17,591
Oh. Uh, Lena went to
a trade conference in Prague

186
00:11:17,799 --> 00:11:20,302
but, uh, you know, I'd be honored.

187
00:11:20,635 --> 00:11:21,845
I thought you guys
weren't having any guests.

188
00:11:21,970 --> 00:11:23,513
Well, we kind of changed our minds.

189
00:11:23,638 --> 00:11:26,141
It's just gonna be a few people--
a dozen, 15.

190
00:11:26,266 --> 00:11:28,059
All right. I'm there.
Where and when?

191
00:11:28,185 --> 00:11:29,603
We don't know yet.
It's nothing fancy.

192
00:11:29,728 --> 00:11:32,480
Oh, well, you have to have it
at our house. I insist.

193
00:11:32,772 --> 00:11:34,566
We have the perfect spot
for a casual wedding.

194
00:11:34,691 --> 00:11:35,734
Really?

195
00:11:36,067 --> 00:11:37,235
I'd be thrilled.

196
00:11:37,569 --> 00:11:38,987
That is so nice of you.

197
00:11:46,912 --> 00:11:48,830
- What's up?
- Some surprise, huh?

198
00:11:49,623 --> 00:11:51,499
I didn't see the wedding thing coming.

199
00:11:52,375 --> 00:11:53,460
It wasn't that hard to guess.

200
00:11:59,591 --> 00:12:01,551
- Something on your mind?
- No.

201
00:12:05,513 --> 00:12:06,806
Actually, yes.

202
00:12:07,724 --> 00:12:10,143
Someone might get in touch with you
about me requesting a transfer.

203
00:12:10,268 --> 00:12:11,978
I just wanted you to hear it
from me first.

204
00:12:12,103 --> 00:12:13,396
- A transfer where?
- Salt Lake.

205
00:12:13,605 --> 00:12:15,398
Office there is starting
a cyber-crime initiative.

206
00:12:15,523 --> 00:12:16,566
They're looking for people.

207
00:12:16,691 --> 00:12:19,444
It's desk work,
but it's more my speed, I think.

208
00:12:23,615 --> 00:12:26,243
Uh, let's face it, I didn't do that well
when we were going after Keller.

209
00:12:26,368 --> 00:12:29,913
It's not easy being in the bullpen.
Michelle's desk is right there, and...

210
00:12:30,914 --> 00:12:32,958
Anyway, I think a change of pace
would be good.

211
00:12:33,541 --> 00:12:35,001
Plus, you're gonna be rebuilding
the team.

212
00:12:35,126 --> 00:12:36,586
This'll pretty much
give you a blank slate.

213
00:12:37,379 --> 00:12:39,172
- Come here.
- What?

214
00:12:39,756 --> 00:12:40,924
Come here.

215
00:12:46,054 --> 00:12:47,847
- Stop feeling sorry for yourself.
- No, I'm not.

216
00:12:47,973 --> 00:12:49,140
You are.

217
00:12:49,432 --> 00:12:51,768
You made some mistakes going
after Keller? Welcome to the club.

218
00:12:52,519 --> 00:12:54,187
I bat 300 on a good day.

219
00:12:56,106 --> 00:12:57,357
You miss Vega.

220
00:12:58,316 --> 00:12:59,567
Now remember who she was.

221
00:13:00,402 --> 00:13:02,737
She'd never run away from a challenge
like this and neither should you.

222
00:13:06,366 --> 00:13:07,450
And you're right.

223
00:13:08,159 --> 00:13:11,121
I have to rebuild the team and I wanna
start with people that I know and trust.

224
00:13:11,997 --> 00:13:14,499
- So stick around.
- Or what, you'll hit me again?

225
00:13:16,126 --> 00:13:17,335
I'm asking you to stay, Wylie.

226
00:13:22,632 --> 00:13:25,176
- Okay.
- Okay, good.

227
00:13:27,262 --> 00:13:28,346
Check in with Tork.

228
00:13:28,471 --> 00:13:29,556
I wanna know what's going on
at the house.

229
00:13:29,681 --> 00:13:31,349
Sure. And Cho...

230
00:13:34,311 --> 00:13:36,313
- Thanks.
- No problem.

231
00:13:40,908 --> 00:13:43,161
This is the ring we sent you
a picture of.

232
00:13:43,286 --> 00:13:44,454
It was my grandmother's.

233
00:13:44,579 --> 00:13:46,372
Anne's dad gave it
to me to propose with.

234
00:13:46,497 --> 00:13:49,667
Which is sweet, but it's not
really me, you know?

235
00:13:49,792 --> 00:13:51,794
So we thought maybe we could
take the diamond out

236
00:13:51,919 --> 00:13:53,463
put it in a necklace or something.

237
00:13:53,838 --> 00:13:55,882
Of course. Uh, may I--
may I see it?

238
00:13:56,007 --> 00:13:57,050
Oh, yeah.

239
00:14:00,762 --> 00:14:01,929
Uh, let me get my loupe.

240
00:14:02,055 --> 00:14:03,806
We'll just need to take
a closer look at the stone.

241
00:14:04,182 --> 00:14:05,224
Excuse me, sir.

242
00:14:05,350 --> 00:14:06,809
I'm helping another customer
right now, sir.

243
00:14:06,976 --> 00:14:08,728
FBI--
give 'em back their ring right now

244
00:14:08,853 --> 00:14:10,438
or I will be forced to shoot you.

245
00:14:11,522 --> 00:14:13,149
Don't worry. Just kidding.

246
00:14:13,316 --> 00:14:14,567
I don't even carry a real gun.

247
00:14:14,692 --> 00:14:16,152
I have a lotta close friends
that do, though.

248
00:14:16,319 --> 00:14:18,279
- What's happening?
- All will be revealed.

249
00:14:18,404 --> 00:14:20,948
- Their ring is in your right hand.
- Uh, sir, you've made a mistake.

250
00:14:21,074 --> 00:14:23,493
- We've got the ring right here.
- Uh, that's a replica.

251
00:14:23,618 --> 00:14:24,661
A... replica?

252
00:14:24,786 --> 00:14:28,039
He did a French drop to swap
the valuable ring with a cheap replica.

253
00:14:28,164 --> 00:14:30,708
French drop is a sleight-of-hand move.
Not important.

254
00:14:30,917 --> 00:14:33,169
That ring never belonged
to your grandmother

255
00:14:33,294 --> 00:14:34,837
and it's not a real diamond.

256
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:37,006
- Is that true?
- Of course not.

257
00:14:37,173 --> 00:14:39,092
He would study the ring
that he just gave you

258
00:14:39,258 --> 00:14:42,679
then break the sad news that
your grandma's ring is a phony

259
00:14:43,012 --> 00:14:44,138
and you'd be none the wiser.

260
00:14:44,597 --> 00:14:45,640
This is insane.

261
00:14:45,765 --> 00:14:47,975
Then you won't mind opening up
your right hand, will you?

262
00:14:50,812 --> 00:14:52,522
Open up your right hand, please, sir.

263
00:14:54,941 --> 00:14:55,983
Holy moly.

264
00:14:56,109 --> 00:14:58,569
Well, thank you for your assistance, folks.
I'll take it from here.

265
00:14:59,821 --> 00:15:02,198
Don't worry, ma'am.
The real ring is in your hand.

266
00:15:02,657 --> 00:15:04,200
- Good day to you.
- Thank you.

267
00:15:04,325 --> 00:15:05,368
My pleasure.

268
00:15:07,662 --> 00:15:10,873
So, my crooked friend,
today is your lucky day.

269
00:15:10,998 --> 00:15:12,458
- Is it?
- Well, on a normal day

270
00:15:12,583 --> 00:15:15,169
you'd be off to the pokey now
but as it happens...

271
00:15:16,212 --> 00:15:17,755
I'm in the market for a diamond ring.

272
00:15:20,633 --> 00:15:22,468
So show me
your very best selection, please.

273
00:15:22,593 --> 00:15:26,472
And, sir, if I see any glass...

274
00:15:27,098 --> 00:15:28,558
the cuffs will come out.

275
00:15:30,059 --> 00:15:31,644
Nothing too gauche.

276
00:15:39,694 --> 00:15:40,737
What's up?

277
00:15:40,862 --> 00:15:41,988
Tork just called in from the crime scene.

278
00:15:42,113 --> 00:15:43,489
No intact corpses in the basement

279
00:15:43,614 --> 00:15:45,950
but a lotta body parts,
badly burned and fragmented.

280
00:15:46,325 --> 00:15:48,870
Have them rush the DNA tests.
Pull some strings if you have to.

281
00:15:49,746 --> 00:15:50,788
Why the rush?

282
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,415
Still got a lotta media interest.

283
00:15:52,540 --> 00:15:54,459
The bosses wanna be able
to announce we got the guy.

284
00:15:54,959 --> 00:15:57,211
For that, we need a coroner's report,
so let's get on it.

285
00:15:57,378 --> 00:15:58,421
Okay, right away.

286
00:16:00,965 --> 00:16:03,134
- Hey, did Abbott give you the news?
- Hey.

287
00:16:03,259 --> 00:16:04,844
We're having a real wedding
at his house.

288
00:16:05,219 --> 00:16:06,804
- He did.
- You're gonna be there, right?

289
00:16:06,929 --> 00:16:07,972
Of course.

290
00:16:08,181 --> 00:16:10,349
I could use your help with something
if you're not too busy.

291
00:16:10,641 --> 00:16:11,684
What's that?

292
00:16:16,898 --> 00:16:18,107
What do you think?

293
00:16:20,985 --> 00:16:22,236
Makes you look short.

294
00:16:32,538 --> 00:16:33,581
Snow cone.

295
00:16:42,048 --> 00:16:43,090
Slutty elf.

296
00:16:44,550 --> 00:16:45,718
You want a simple piece
with clean lines

297
00:16:45,843 --> 00:16:47,345
maybe something vintage
and off-white.

298
00:16:47,678 --> 00:16:48,721
What he said.

299
00:16:50,473 --> 00:16:51,849
Thank you for doing this.

300
00:16:51,974 --> 00:16:53,768
I asked you along
'cause I thought you'd be honest.

301
00:16:53,893 --> 00:16:56,604
I had no idea you were such
a fashion expert.

302
00:16:56,729 --> 00:16:57,772
Not me.

303
00:16:57,897 --> 00:16:59,732
My mom could run up
a designer gown before breakfast.

304
00:16:59,857 --> 00:17:01,192
- Cut her cloth by eye.
- Cool.

305
00:17:01,317 --> 00:17:03,361
My mom had a sewing machine,
but it was always in hock.

306
00:17:05,112 --> 00:17:06,489
She'd be very proud of you.

307
00:17:06,656 --> 00:17:07,782
Looking like this?

308
00:17:08,866 --> 00:17:10,117
Very proud.

309
00:17:11,410 --> 00:17:12,870
Thank you, Kimball.

310
00:17:16,999 --> 00:17:18,459
All right, good night, Wade.

311
00:17:18,584 --> 00:17:21,295
And, uh, tell Shaniqua
I said thanks for the fan mail.

312
00:17:37,186 --> 00:17:38,229
Excuse me.

313
00:17:39,522 --> 00:17:40,606
I-I don't have any change, man.

314
00:17:40,898 --> 00:17:43,860
Hey, hey, hey!
Hey. Okay. Okay. Okay.

315
00:17:44,944 --> 00:17:47,029
Here, look. You can take it.
You can take it. Here.

316
00:17:47,154 --> 00:17:48,364
Get in the car.

317
00:17:50,241 --> 00:17:51,951
Do as I say and you won't get hurt.

318
00:18:19,126 --> 00:18:20,460
Stop the vehicle.

319
00:18:20,919 --> 00:18:22,671
"Very slowly. No one gets hurt."

320
00:18:24,589 --> 00:18:26,967
Put the car in park and get out.

321
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:30,762
Easy.

322
00:18:33,098 --> 00:18:34,141
Easy.

323
00:18:40,647 --> 00:18:41,732
Give me your phone.

324
00:18:42,232 --> 00:18:43,275
All right.

325
00:18:44,693 --> 00:18:45,736
No problems.

326
00:18:46,987 --> 00:18:48,071
What's the passcode?

327
00:18:48,697 --> 00:18:49,823
There isn't any.

328
00:18:52,409 --> 00:18:53,493
Wallet.

329
00:18:54,703 --> 00:18:56,913
Look, uh, I only got
about 20 bucks in it.

330
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:58,373
And, uh...

331
00:18:59,916 --> 00:19:01,460
Would you let me keep
my driver's license?

332
00:19:02,044 --> 00:19:04,212
I-I don't wanna have to go
to the DMV.

333
00:19:04,921 --> 00:19:05,964
Sure.

334
00:19:12,596 --> 00:19:13,930
Here you go.

335
00:19:14,681 --> 00:19:15,724
Thanks.

336
00:19:16,683 --> 00:19:18,018
Thank you.

337
00:19:19,227 --> 00:19:23,940
No! No! No!
No! No! No!

338
00:19:53,553 --> 00:19:55,972
- Tork.
- Patrick Jane, please.

339
00:19:56,098 --> 00:19:57,516
Um, sorry. He's not in.

340
00:19:57,974 --> 00:19:59,768
This is Dan Glover
from Austin Today.

341
00:19:59,893 --> 00:20:02,354
I interviewed Jane recently
about this whole Lazarus case.

342
00:20:02,604 --> 00:20:03,647
Sure. I remember you.

343
00:20:04,064 --> 00:20:06,358
I just wanna do a quick follow-up.
Is he available?

344
00:20:06,525 --> 00:20:08,902
I'm afraid, uh, you're gonna have
to wait a few days on that.

345
00:20:09,027 --> 00:20:10,237
He's outta the office for a while.

346
00:20:10,362 --> 00:20:12,572
Can you tell me where I can find him?
It'll only take a few moments.

347
00:20:12,697 --> 00:20:14,783
I'd say he's pretty unfindable
at the moment.

348
00:20:14,908 --> 00:20:16,243
"He's getting married in a few days."

349
00:20:16,368 --> 00:20:17,661
- Married?
- Yeah.

350
00:20:18,328 --> 00:20:20,664
I can, uh, take a message,
tell him you called.

351
00:20:20,789 --> 00:20:22,999
No, no need.

352
00:20:23,708 --> 00:20:24,751
Okey-doke.

353
00:20:31,383 --> 00:20:32,426
Huh.

354
00:20:42,727 --> 00:20:45,897
If I just remembered how tedious
this aspect of the marriage is

355
00:20:46,022 --> 00:20:47,441
I might not have asked you.

356
00:20:47,941 --> 00:20:49,901
No, seriously. I'm only on page two.

357
00:20:50,110 --> 00:20:52,404
You know, I could just give you
the ring and we could elope.

358
00:20:52,821 --> 00:20:54,364
Don't be mean. No take-backs.

359
00:20:56,241 --> 00:20:59,786
I could give you this
and we could be in Fiji by nightfall.

360
00:20:59,911 --> 00:21:02,497
There are people coming.
We're getting married, damn it.

361
00:21:02,831 --> 00:21:04,541
- Suit yourself.
- You got a ring?

362
00:21:04,666 --> 00:21:05,709
Yes, I did.

363
00:21:06,585 --> 00:21:08,336
- You gonna show it to me?
- You wanna see it?

364
00:21:08,503 --> 00:21:09,546
Show me.

365
00:21:11,381 --> 00:21:13,592
I'll take this,
and you'll fill all of this out.

366
00:21:18,555 --> 00:21:21,099
Oh, my God.
It's not real. You scared me.

367
00:21:21,224 --> 00:21:22,684
- It's funny.
- Of course it's real.

368
00:21:23,018 --> 00:21:24,686
- It's real?
- Real.

369
00:21:27,272 --> 00:21:29,900
Oh, my--
Are you outta your mind?

370
00:21:30,066 --> 00:21:31,109
You like it?

371
00:21:31,234 --> 00:21:33,278
Well, it's gorgeous, but it's too much.

372
00:21:34,154 --> 00:21:35,530
I-I can't accept it.

373
00:21:36,406 --> 00:21:38,116
You can accept it, and you will.

374
00:21:38,241 --> 00:21:39,910
It's yours. I want you to have it.

375
00:21:40,118 --> 00:21:41,828
What is the Justice of the Peace's name?

376
00:21:41,995 --> 00:21:43,121
Emily Hamilton.

377
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:47,042
- Oh, my...
- All right, let's file this sucker.

378
00:21:48,168 --> 00:21:51,421
All right. We'll need confirmation
that the ceremony's been performed

379
00:21:51,588 --> 00:21:54,549
within 72 hours, or you will need
to refile.

380
00:21:55,217 --> 00:21:56,426
Congratulations.

381
00:21:56,843 --> 00:21:59,221
- Who said romance is dead?
- I can't take this.

382
00:21:59,387 --> 00:22:00,722
No, not yet you can't.

383
00:22:01,389 --> 00:22:02,682
Well, at least let me try it on.

384
00:22:02,807 --> 00:22:04,684
- Not yet.
- We don't even know if it fits!

385
00:22:11,274 --> 00:22:12,692
- Lisbon, hi.
- Yes!

386
00:22:12,817 --> 00:22:14,569
- Wylie, did we invite you yet?
- No, not yet.

387
00:22:14,736 --> 00:22:18,073
Well, here it is.
Abbott's house, 12:00 Saturday.

388
00:22:18,281 --> 00:22:20,367
But try not to spread it around.
We wanna keep it small.

389
00:22:20,492 --> 00:22:21,701
And I don't wanna hurt
anybody's feelings.

390
00:22:21,826 --> 00:22:24,371
I got you. Is there a gift registry?

391
00:22:24,538 --> 00:22:26,790
- Uh, no gifts.
- Is there a trousseau?

392
00:22:26,915 --> 00:22:29,292
- I don't know. What is that exactly?
- Never mind.

393
00:22:31,419 --> 00:22:33,088
You're coming back
to work, right? Here?

394
00:22:33,213 --> 00:22:35,382
Yeah, I think so.

395
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:38,677
- Why are you whispering?
- Lisbon, hey.

396
00:22:39,177 --> 00:22:40,220
Someone's trying to reach you.

397
00:22:41,846 --> 00:22:42,889
Oh, my God.

398
00:22:43,390 --> 00:22:44,933
- "Hey, boss."
- "Hi."

399
00:22:45,517 --> 00:22:48,728
- I'll talk to you guys later, okay?
- It is so good to see you guys.

400
00:22:48,895 --> 00:22:50,021
"Right back at ya."

401
00:22:50,188 --> 00:22:53,233
"Well, the news is spreading fast
through the CBI grapevine."

402
00:22:53,358 --> 00:22:55,026
- "It's true, isn't it?"
- It's true.

403
00:22:55,402 --> 00:22:57,404
"Oh, well, we had to call
and say congratulations."

404
00:22:57,862 --> 00:23:00,907
"So, you and Jane, huh?
We always knew."

405
00:23:01,283 --> 00:23:02,909
"We always knew?
I always knew."

406
00:23:03,034 --> 00:23:04,077
How are the kids?

407
00:23:04,244 --> 00:23:06,997
- "Uh, sticky, mostly."
- "The kids are great."

408
00:23:07,122 --> 00:23:09,749
I know it's short notice, but you guys
have gotta come out for the wedding.

409
00:23:09,916 --> 00:23:10,959
It's Saturday.

410
00:23:11,084 --> 00:23:12,711
"Oh, my gosh, of course.
We'd love to."

411
00:23:12,877 --> 00:23:15,422
"It will take a little child-care juggling
but we can swing it."

412
00:23:15,589 --> 00:23:17,382
"You know, worst comes to worst
we'll just bring the little monkeys with us."

413
00:23:17,549 --> 00:23:19,593
- "Keep 'em locked in the rental car."
- "Will not."

414
00:23:19,759 --> 00:23:21,553
- "I'm kidding."
- "Mommy!"

415
00:23:21,928 --> 00:23:23,513
"No, but seriously, we wouldn't
miss it for anything."

416
00:23:24,014 --> 00:23:25,307
"I gotta go. We'll see you soon."

417
00:23:25,557 --> 00:23:26,891
All right, I'll send you the details.

418
00:23:27,058 --> 00:23:28,268
"Great. Take care."

419
00:23:43,033 --> 00:23:45,660
Okay, you guys are all set. It should be
in the mail three to five days.

420
00:23:46,161 --> 00:23:47,203
Thanks.

421
00:23:50,540 --> 00:23:52,584
Excuse me. I need to fill out
a marriage license.

422
00:23:54,628 --> 00:23:56,838
Um, usually there's two of you.

423
00:23:57,505 --> 00:23:59,299
She's running late. I'll get started.

424
00:23:59,841 --> 00:24:02,260
Okay, well, uh, paperwork
is in the end tray.

425
00:24:02,427 --> 00:24:05,096
Just fill that out.
We need both of you here, plus ID.

426
00:24:05,263 --> 00:24:06,306
I see.

427
00:24:06,765 --> 00:24:08,308
Will do, thanks.

428
00:24:22,906 --> 00:24:24,699
City Clerk's office. Please hold.

429
00:24:25,617 --> 00:24:27,369
Thanks for holding.
Yes, how may I help you?

430
00:24:28,411 --> 00:24:30,163
No, ma'am. You can't file online.

431
00:24:31,122 --> 00:24:33,416
Until six, but we're closed
from twelve to one.

432
00:24:34,125 --> 00:24:35,168
You're welcome.

433
00:24:41,132 --> 00:24:44,803
Looks like she stood me up.
Bad omen for a wedding, huh?

434
00:24:54,270 --> 00:24:55,313
Abbott.

435
00:24:56,773 --> 00:24:57,816
Can I run something by you?

436
00:24:58,566 --> 00:24:59,609
Yeah, shoot.

437
00:24:59,943 --> 00:25:02,362
Spot DNA test came back
from the Keller house.

438
00:25:02,779 --> 00:25:06,700
So far, all the recovered body parts
belong to Joe Senior, none for Junior.

439
00:25:06,825 --> 00:25:08,451
They found his gun, but not him.

440
00:25:08,618 --> 00:25:10,912
Oh, damn.

441
00:25:11,121 --> 00:25:14,207
It could be that he was at the epicenter
of the explosion and was vaporized.

442
00:25:14,332 --> 00:25:18,086
But there's a strong possibility
that Keller, A.K.A. Lazarus, is still alive.

443
00:25:18,628 --> 00:25:19,671
Damn.

444
00:25:19,838 --> 00:25:21,423
I let Austin PD know

445
00:25:21,548 --> 00:25:23,675
and we're putting out a BOLO
to all the local hospitals.

446
00:25:24,008 --> 00:25:25,510
Wylie's putting together a KA list

447
00:25:25,635 --> 00:25:27,178
and I'm gonna have agents set up
shop at all of them.

448
00:25:27,303 --> 00:25:29,973
- Well, did you put out a wire just in case--
- He runs for the border, yeah.

449
00:25:32,434 --> 00:25:34,686
All right, well, it seems like
you have everything handled.

450
00:25:37,897 --> 00:25:39,858
I don't know if I should tell
Jane and Lisbon.

451
00:25:39,983 --> 00:25:41,443
- Good question.
- Yeah.

452
00:25:44,821 --> 00:25:45,947
I wouldn't.

453
00:25:46,489 --> 00:25:48,116
We don't have enough to be sure.

454
00:25:48,241 --> 00:25:50,326
And, you know, they're
in a good space right now.

455
00:25:50,452 --> 00:25:53,079
If Lisbon found out
that this case isn't closed

456
00:25:53,204 --> 00:25:56,082
it's likely that she'll cancel the wedding
and join the hunt.

457
00:25:56,958 --> 00:25:59,294
Yeah, there's plenty of time
to tell them after.

458
00:26:00,795 --> 00:26:03,757
But, if he's still alive...

459
00:26:03,882 --> 00:26:05,425
You know, Keller's unpredictable

460
00:26:06,426 --> 00:26:08,094
and Jane did try to kill him.

461
00:26:09,679 --> 00:26:10,889
You know, just in case

462
00:26:11,014 --> 00:26:13,808
why don't we put some bodies
at the wedding

463
00:26:13,933 --> 00:26:15,268
just to keep an eye out.

464
00:26:15,518 --> 00:26:17,312
And it's my house,
so I'll arrange it.

465
00:26:17,437 --> 00:26:18,480
You sure?

466
00:26:18,605 --> 00:26:20,690
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
It's something to keep me busy.

467
00:26:21,274 --> 00:26:22,525
Okay, thanks.

468
00:26:24,027 --> 00:26:25,487
Abbott said it's totally up to you

469
00:26:25,612 --> 00:26:28,156
but that you'd probably prefer
to hold the ceremony outside

470
00:26:28,281 --> 00:26:29,991
and there isn't really
a room inside big enough.

471
00:26:30,241 --> 00:26:31,743
Well, how many people
are we talking about?

472
00:26:31,868 --> 00:26:33,495
Oh! A lotta people are talking about it.

473
00:26:34,078 --> 00:26:36,247
Well, we only invited like 15 people.

474
00:26:36,498 --> 00:26:40,210
Mm... more like 25 or--
I know.

475
00:26:40,376 --> 00:26:43,463
And I don't think people
are waiting for, like a printed invitation...

476
00:26:43,588 --> 00:26:45,590
seeing as there isn't one.

477
00:26:46,174 --> 00:26:48,718
But, hey, on the plus side,
you're popular, girl!

478
00:26:49,135 --> 00:26:50,595
Is that what all these tables are for?

479
00:26:50,720 --> 00:26:51,971
Yeah, Abbott thought they'd be useful.

480
00:26:52,096 --> 00:26:53,223
Don't worry.
He's covering the rental...

481
00:26:53,973 --> 00:26:55,016
and the bartender...

482
00:26:55,683 --> 00:26:56,935
and the caterer.

483
00:26:57,060 --> 00:26:59,437
I guess they're his wedding gift.
I don't know.

484
00:26:59,604 --> 00:27:00,647
Hey, here's a menu.

485
00:27:01,064 --> 00:27:03,608
- There's a caterer?
- Yeah. Yeah, it's fine.

486
00:27:04,067 --> 00:27:06,569
Abbott's loaded.
I mean, look at this house.

487
00:27:06,736 --> 00:27:08,530
I think his wife cleaned up
in the private sector.

488
00:27:08,655 --> 00:27:09,739
Wow.

489
00:27:09,864 --> 00:27:12,492
"Here we are.
Hey, everybody out."

490
00:27:12,617 --> 00:27:14,410
- Hey, Teresa!
- Hey!

491
00:27:14,994 --> 00:27:16,371
- We're here!
- Hey-hey!

492
00:27:16,746 --> 00:27:17,789
T!

493
00:27:18,873 --> 00:27:21,084
Hi! Wow!

494
00:27:21,793 --> 00:27:24,838
- You all came! So many people.
- Yeah, hey.

495
00:27:24,963 --> 00:27:26,840
Sure we came.
We're gonna let our sister down?

496
00:27:30,009 --> 00:27:31,594
- Congratulations.
- Thanks.

497
00:27:31,719 --> 00:27:33,471
Yeah, hey, guys, say hi to your
Aunt Teresa, all right?

498
00:27:33,596 --> 00:27:35,139
- Hi!
- Hi!

499
00:27:35,306 --> 00:27:38,309
- Who is this?
- Oh, T, this is Lucy, my fiancée.

500
00:27:38,726 --> 00:27:39,853
Lucy, Teresa.

501
00:27:39,978 --> 00:27:42,605
I am so freaked out to meet you at last.

502
00:27:42,772 --> 00:27:45,900
- We're gonna be sisters! Yay!
- Yay!

503
00:27:46,025 --> 00:27:47,235
It's a long story.

504
00:27:49,487 --> 00:27:51,990
- So, you're all here. Welcome to Austin.
- Thanks.

505
00:27:52,115 --> 00:27:53,658
Yeah, it looks like we brought
the weather with us.

506
00:27:54,075 --> 00:27:55,159
FBI!

507
00:27:56,035 --> 00:27:58,955
- Sorry, I'm freaking out right now.
- Yeah, we got that.

508
00:27:59,581 --> 00:28:00,915
- Excuse me?
- You all came.

509
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:03,501
- Yeah. Already said that, T.
- Let's go in!

510
00:28:03,918 --> 00:28:06,546
- Jason! Jason! Come here!
- Yeah! Okay.

511
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:09,215
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

512
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:27,163
Uh, excuse me, sir.

513
00:28:27,372 --> 00:28:28,832
We have an odd coincidence...

514
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:32,002
Or not. Maybe.

515
00:28:32,293 --> 00:28:34,170
Austin PD got a missing-person's report

516
00:28:34,337 --> 00:28:36,881
on a local television reporter
named Dan Glover.

517
00:28:37,007 --> 00:28:38,174
The one that interviewed Jane.

518
00:28:38,299 --> 00:28:41,428
Yeah, left work Thursday night,
hasn't been seen since.

519
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:44,639
The weird thing is, he called here
right around the time he was last seen.

520
00:28:44,764 --> 00:28:47,225
I spoke to him. He said
he wanted to interview Jane again

521
00:28:47,350 --> 00:28:49,352
and I said he was unavailable
because he was getting...

522
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:51,730
married.

523
00:28:52,647 --> 00:28:54,774
So, you're not even sure
if you spoke to Glover?

524
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:57,736
No, I mean, I was certain
at the time.

525
00:28:57,861 --> 00:28:59,904
Obviously, it was his caller ID
but now--

526
00:29:00,071 --> 00:29:02,449
So, we have to assume
the killer's alive and looking for Jane.

527
00:29:03,324 --> 00:29:04,993
How many agents are you gonna have
at the wedding?

528
00:29:05,452 --> 00:29:08,079
Four, but now I think
we should probably have more.

529
00:29:08,246 --> 00:29:09,289
At least 10.

530
00:29:09,414 --> 00:29:10,749
We're gonna need eyes
on the front and backyards

531
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:12,167
and the surrounding neighborhoods.

532
00:29:12,417 --> 00:29:14,627
We should have a chopper on standby
in case we need to pursue.

533
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:15,795
Yes, sir.

534
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:18,798
But wouldn't it be wiser
to just postpone the wedding?

535
00:29:19,799 --> 00:29:22,427
Postpone the wedding?
We're the FBI.

536
00:29:23,303 --> 00:29:25,221
There is that upside.

537
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:28,725
We can use the wedding as bait...
kind of.

538
00:29:31,853 --> 00:29:33,146
I'm gonna go check on that chopper.

539
00:29:35,774 --> 00:29:37,692
Still think we shouldn't tell
Jane and Lisbon?

540
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:40,653
We're the FBI.

541
00:29:41,196 --> 00:29:43,198
Just like you said, we can handle it.

542
00:29:49,079 --> 00:29:50,121
Abbott.

543
00:29:50,872 --> 00:29:51,915
Hey.

544
00:29:54,751 --> 00:29:57,128
What were you and Cho and Tork
huddled about?

545
00:29:59,005 --> 00:30:00,173
Nothing special.

546
00:30:01,174 --> 00:30:02,300
Nothing special
that's keeping you here

547
00:30:02,467 --> 00:30:04,427
when you could be in Prague
with your lovely wife?

548
00:30:06,471 --> 00:30:08,598
You know, she doesn't need me around.
I...

549
00:30:08,932 --> 00:30:10,100
I get in the way.

550
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:12,644
You're lying to me.
I won't pursue the point

551
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:15,146
because you would tell me
if it was something important.

552
00:30:15,355 --> 00:30:16,731
Oh, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, of course.

553
00:30:16,856 --> 00:30:19,400
If-if I thought that it was something
that we couldn't handle.

554
00:30:20,318 --> 00:30:22,028
You know, um...

555
00:30:24,906 --> 00:30:26,866
I've been getting some calls about you

556
00:30:27,075 --> 00:30:29,119
and my bosses wanna know
if you're sticking around.

557
00:30:29,244 --> 00:30:30,286
That's a good question.

558
00:30:32,747 --> 00:30:34,165
All right, well, no pressure.

559
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:36,126
But if you're going

560
00:30:36,251 --> 00:30:38,211
there is some legal stuff
that we need to handle

561
00:30:38,711 --> 00:30:40,547
to expunge that deal that we made.

562
00:30:41,047 --> 00:30:42,132
The napkin?

563
00:30:46,678 --> 00:30:48,263
I'm getting married tomorrow.

564
00:30:49,556 --> 00:30:51,307
Then I'm building a house, and...

565
00:30:52,225 --> 00:30:55,436
beyond that
I genuinely have no idea.

566
00:30:56,729 --> 00:30:58,731
And I can't do this job forever

567
00:31:00,024 --> 00:31:01,776
but it's gonna be tough to give up.

568
00:31:01,901 --> 00:31:04,195
Yeah, it's hard giving up
making a difference, huh?

569
00:31:04,404 --> 00:31:06,114
No, everyone makes a difference.

570
00:31:06,781 --> 00:31:09,325
- Hard to give up the chase.
- Oh, yeah.

571
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:12,579
That it is.

572
00:31:16,124 --> 00:31:19,335
So, you, uh, let me know
when you know.

573
00:31:19,460 --> 00:31:20,628
I will.

574
00:31:22,797 --> 00:31:25,258
It has been very good
working with you, Patrick.

575
00:31:26,050 --> 00:31:27,802
You too, Dennis.

576
00:31:28,094 --> 00:31:29,929
I really appreciate your honesty.

577
00:31:30,263 --> 00:31:31,598
I love you for that.

578
00:31:33,099 --> 00:31:34,184
Thank you.

579
00:31:43,109 --> 00:31:44,485
Okay, you got me. I was lying.

580
00:31:44,611 --> 00:31:46,279
There is something
I need to talk to you about.

581
00:32:03,087 --> 00:32:04,964
- Hey.
- Hi.

582
00:32:05,465 --> 00:32:06,633
Nice flowers.

583
00:32:07,842 --> 00:32:09,177
They're centerpieces.

584
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:13,598
- It's a Sylvan theme.
- Sylvan theme.

585
00:32:14,390 --> 00:32:15,934
All right. Cool, I guess.

586
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:19,938
How many... people are
actually coming to this thing?

587
00:32:20,355 --> 00:32:22,065
Nobody knows exactly.

588
00:32:24,442 --> 00:32:25,568
Okay.

589
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:29,614
How did this happen?
This is not what I wanted.

590
00:32:31,574 --> 00:32:32,951
Well, I like the Sylvan theme.

591
00:32:33,076 --> 00:32:34,994
We should've just eloped
like you said.

592
00:32:36,996 --> 00:32:39,165
- What about your family?
- Oh, they wouldn't care.

593
00:32:39,290 --> 00:32:41,542
I just talked to them at the hotel.
They found a minibar.

594
00:32:41,668 --> 00:32:44,504
They're like cavemen
arguing over a dead antelope.

595
00:32:44,629 --> 00:32:46,297
All right, well, uh...

596
00:32:46,756 --> 00:32:48,883
Let's run, huh?

597
00:32:49,217 --> 00:32:51,970
We'll tell nobody, just the judge.

598
00:32:52,262 --> 00:32:55,223
I'll have her meet us
at our little cabin tomorrow morning.

599
00:32:55,431 --> 00:32:57,350
- The cabin?
- Just us.

600
00:32:57,976 --> 00:32:59,269
What, you think the judge
would do that?

601
00:32:59,394 --> 00:33:01,938
Well, sure. I mean, she's driving in
from San Antonio tonight.

602
00:33:02,063 --> 00:33:03,606
Change of venue makes
no difference to her.

603
00:33:03,731 --> 00:33:06,859
- Well, what about the witnesses?
- We'll get someone... Park ranger.

604
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:10,154
- You know what? Let's do it.
- Yeah.

605
00:33:10,280 --> 00:33:11,322
- It's our life, damn it.
- Yes.

606
00:33:11,447 --> 00:33:13,283
- I love you. Thank you.
- I love you, too.

607
00:33:13,408 --> 00:33:14,492
- Hey, there's a--
- I'm gonna go get my dress

608
00:33:14,617 --> 00:33:16,160
and I'm gonna go to the Airstream.
I'll meet you there.

609
00:33:16,327 --> 00:33:19,998
Well, there's another very good reason
why we should elope, all right?

610
00:33:20,123 --> 00:33:23,293
Keller is apparently still alive
and he's mad at me for some reason.

611
00:33:24,711 --> 00:33:27,797
- Oh, my God.
- Yeah, so Cho and his people

612
00:33:27,922 --> 00:33:29,382
are gonna stake out this house.

613
00:33:29,549 --> 00:33:31,342
When Keller shows up, they'll nab him.

614
00:33:31,467 --> 00:33:33,136
You were gonna withhold
this information from me?

615
00:33:33,261 --> 00:33:35,638
You were gonna deprive me
of a guilt-free elopement?

616
00:33:35,930 --> 00:33:38,057
- I just told you.
- You almost didn't!

617
00:33:38,349 --> 00:33:40,768
From now on, we need to be
100% honest with each other.

618
00:33:40,935 --> 00:33:42,770
- I agree with you 100%.
- Okay.

619
00:33:43,104 --> 00:33:44,814
- Honesty.
- I am gonna go get my dress.

620
00:33:44,939 --> 00:33:46,774
- Fire up the Airstream.
- You go, girl.

621
00:33:52,697 --> 00:33:54,741
Hi. Judge Hamilton, Patrick Jane.

622
00:33:55,074 --> 00:33:57,160
Uh, there's been a change of venue.

623
00:33:57,952 --> 00:34:00,705
Okay. No problem, Mr. Jane.

624
00:34:00,830 --> 00:34:04,375
If you just text me the exact address
and perhaps a decent motel nearby.

625
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:05,543
I'll see you tomorrow.

626
00:34:06,294 --> 00:34:07,545
Great. Bye.

627
00:34:45,291 --> 00:34:46,667
We got four agents on the roof

628
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:48,628
five dressed as catering and valet service

629
00:34:48,961 --> 00:34:50,004
six on the perimeter

630
00:34:50,129 --> 00:34:52,215
and six undercover mobiles
covering the approach roads.

631
00:34:53,049 --> 00:34:54,092
When the guests get here

632
00:34:54,217 --> 00:34:56,344
I'll gather them inside
and explain the situation.

633
00:34:56,469 --> 00:34:58,805
Most of them are law enforcement
so they'll understand.

634
00:34:59,847 --> 00:35:00,973
What is it, Wylie?

635
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:02,809
Office got a call off the BOLO
from a clerk

636
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:04,560
at the South Austin Registry Office.

637
00:35:04,685 --> 00:35:06,687
A man with extensive burns
came in yesterday

638
00:35:06,813 --> 00:35:08,231
and pretended to fill out a form.

639
00:35:08,356 --> 00:35:09,732
The clerk thinks
he may have taken a peek

640
00:35:09,857 --> 00:35:11,609
at the marriage-license forms
on her desk.

641
00:35:11,984 --> 00:35:14,112
So that confirms it.
He is coming to the wedding.

642
00:35:14,362 --> 00:35:16,155
Well, we got it covered.
Why are you so anxious, Wylie?

643
00:35:16,364 --> 00:35:18,908
I know all the state forms from
when I used to work downtown.

644
00:35:19,075 --> 00:35:21,577
The marriage-license form
doesn't ask where the wedding is.

645
00:35:21,702 --> 00:35:24,205
- It just asks who the officiant is.
- Well, that's the judge.

646
00:35:24,330 --> 00:35:25,373
Yeah.

647
00:36:06,038 --> 00:36:07,957
- Hey, you.
- Hi.

648
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:16,215
Wow.

649
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:21,804
Well, no matter what happens,
from this point on

650
00:36:23,723 --> 00:36:25,475
we have to promise each other that...

651
00:36:26,309 --> 00:36:28,102
we will always
look on the bright side.

652
00:36:28,561 --> 00:36:29,687
I promise.

653
00:36:33,149 --> 00:36:34,192
Me too.

654
00:37:20,655 --> 00:37:22,490
Freeze! Drop the gun!

655
00:37:32,708 --> 00:37:35,545
And see how much better things turn out
when you're honest with me?

656
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:36,712
Thank you.

657
00:37:37,421 --> 00:37:38,506
Let's do this.

658
00:37:39,549 --> 00:37:40,591
No hard feelings.

659
00:37:49,897 --> 00:37:53,610
Patrick, do you take Teresa to be
your lawful, wedded wife

660
00:37:53,735 --> 00:37:56,237
to have and to hold
in sickness and health

661
00:37:56,487 --> 00:37:59,616
for better or for worse,
till death do you part?

662
00:38:00,658 --> 00:38:02,035
I sure do.

663
00:38:02,785 --> 00:38:05,079
And, you, Teresa, do you take Patrick

664
00:38:05,204 --> 00:38:06,914
to be your lawful, wedded husband

665
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:09,500
to have and to hold in sickness and health

666
00:38:09,626 --> 00:38:12,670
for better or for worse,
till death do you part?

667
00:38:13,129 --> 00:38:14,297
I do.

668
00:38:15,381 --> 00:38:18,051
Then by the power granted me
by the State of Texas

669
00:38:18,426 --> 00:38:21,262
I declare you husband and wife.

670
00:38:22,138 --> 00:38:23,681
You may kiss the bride.

671
00:38:30,438 --> 00:38:35,526
Ladies and gentlemen,
Patrick and Teresa.

672
00:38:57,882 --> 00:38:59,634
"Do you remember"

673
00:39:00,551 --> 00:39:03,054
"The 21st night of September?"

674
00:39:03,971 --> 00:39:06,891
"Love was changing the minds
of pretenders"

675
00:39:07,850 --> 00:39:11,604
- "While chasing the clouds away"
- Who else is gonna hug me? Come on!

676
00:39:13,398 --> 00:39:15,066
"Our hearts were ringing"

677
00:39:15,316 --> 00:39:18,569
"In the key that our souls were singing"

678
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:22,407
"As we danced in the night, remember"

679
00:39:23,241 --> 00:39:26,786
"How the stars stole the night away?"

680
00:39:31,249 --> 00:39:33,209
"Say, do you remember"

681
00:39:35,044 --> 00:39:37,046
"Dancing in September?"

682
00:39:39,006 --> 00:39:42,677
"Never was a cloudy day"

683
00:39:59,318 --> 00:40:00,862
"My thoughts are with you"

684
00:40:01,237 --> 00:40:04,532
"Holding hands with your heart
to see you"

685
00:40:05,241 --> 00:40:08,119
"Only blue talk and love, remember"

686
00:40:09,036 --> 00:40:12,206
"How we knew love was here to stay?"

687
00:40:14,792 --> 00:40:17,587
"Now, December found the love..."

688
00:40:19,005 --> 00:40:20,047
How you feeling?

689
00:40:22,091 --> 00:40:23,634
I am so happy.

690
00:40:24,635 --> 00:40:26,053
Me too.

691
00:40:28,347 --> 00:40:29,724
Me too.

692
00:40:33,519 --> 00:40:35,938
There's something I need to tell you.

693
00:40:47,241 --> 00:40:49,118
No, you're--
you're kidding me?

694
00:40:49,243 --> 00:40:50,787
I'm not kidding.

695
00:40:56,250 --> 00:40:57,919
You are?

696
00:40:59,045 --> 00:41:00,588
I am.

